---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const DEMO_URL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_DEMO_URL || 'https://shoreline-demo.onrender.com/menu'
---

<BaseLayout title="Founder Story — Built by an Healthcare Chef" description="Why ShorelineOps was created inside a real senior living kitchen dealing with dysphagia textures, allergen risks, and food distributor ordering.">
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-12 sm:mb-16">
        <div class="inline-block px-3.5 py-1 bg-teal-50 dark:bg-teal-950/70 border border-teal-200/70 dark:border-teal-800/60 rounded-full text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 font-mono">
          Practitioner-Led Healthcare Software
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-4 leading-tight">
          Why I Built ShorelineOps Inside a Real Senior Living Kitchen.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 italic">
          "Nobody selling software to senior living has cooked a pureed dinner service for 80 residents with 14 different allergy restrictions."
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          If you’ve ever run a senior living dietary department, you know the daily reality:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>Nursing calls down at 4:30 PM with three new room moves, a new diabetic diet order, and a resident transitioning to Pureed texture.</li>
          <li>Your morning cook is trying to read handwriting on a greasy dry-erase board while balancing 4 pots on the range.</li>
          <li>You’re trying to build your weekly order for <strong>Dennis Food Service</strong> using clipboards and guesswork, hoping you don't run out of thickener before Friday.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4">The Legacy Software Failure</h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
          When I looked at what the software industry offered, I found two extremes:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>Enterprise Monopolies ($1,200+/month)</strong>: Bulky software designed for 500-bed hospital chains, bloated with features no 60-bed assisted living facility will ever touch, and locked into rigid distributor contracts.</li>
          <li><strong>Binders and Clipboards</strong>: What 80% of independent facilities actually use because the alternatives are too expensive or difficult to train staff on.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4">The ShorelineOps Philosophy: Free Software + Paid SaaS</h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
          I built <strong>ShorelineOps</strong> to be the tool I wished I had in the kitchen every morning:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>100% Free Core Software</strong> so community facilities and non-profit homes can operate with complete clinical safety without predatory software fees.</li>
          <li><strong>Big, touch-friendly tablet buttons</strong> that line cooks can tap with gloved hands.</li>
          <li><strong>Bright red allergen & IDDSI banners</strong> that make it impossible to serve the wrong food to a dysphagia resident.</li>
          <li><strong>Suggested Multi-Distributor ordering</strong> that calculates <code>Par Level - On Hand</code> automatically so you never over-order or run short.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 my-8 text-center shadow-apple-card">
          <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Let’s Talk Kitchen Operations</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-xs sm:text-sm max-w-lg mx-auto mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            Whether you’re a Dietary Manager in Maine or an Executive Director looking to tighten food spend, I’d love to show you how we run ShorelineOps.
          </p>
          <a
            href={DEMO_URL}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-xs sm:text-sm transition-all shadow-sm shadow-blue-600/30"
          >
            Launch Interactive Demo App &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
